{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023906-topic-for-discussion-damage-vs-resistant-damage","id":1023906,"title":"Topic for discussion: Damage vs Resistant damage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-29T13:06:58-08:00","id":1023906,"title":"Topic for discussion: Damage vs Resistant damage","content":"I know that when you take damage that the worse damage is put in the left most boxes of your health bar. so if you had 4 bashing damage in the left most boxes and then you take a lethal damage it will most to the beginning of your health bar so that when you heal you heal the bashing first.<br /> <br /> My question is, does bashing damage stay in the box that it occurred in or does it move to the left since it cannot be magically healed. and if it moves how far left does it move? all the way or just to the beginning of its type? And when bashing turns to lethal or lethal to aggravated and you upgrade the one that is resistant is the entire thing resistant or is in only partially resistant. Example. I have taken 4 out of 7 damage and all 4 is bashing, I then take 1 lethal. That lethal moves to the left ahead of the bashing. I then take on resistant bashing from containing paradox. I now have 6 wound levels out of 7, I take -2 wound penalties. Do I move the resistant damage to the left? and if I do does it move all the way to the left to the front of the line displacing the 1 lethal or all the way to the front of just the bashing damage. I the take 2 more bashing that means that I have taken 8 health levels out of 7 health. I now mark the 7th box and then upgrade one of the bashing that I have taken to lethal. If the upgrade lands on the bashing that is resistant is the entire this now resistant?<br /> <br /> Hope I didn't confuse any one more than I am confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T02:48:04-08:00","id":1024174,"title":"","content":"Resistant damage doesn't have special rules for moving left. It moves like any other damage does, but should (since nothing says otherwise) say &quot;linked&quot; to the damage it was originally written down with.<br /> <br /> Basically, the only time you should be moving the mark that something is resistant left is when you've been healed magically but it has to skip that damage because it's resistant.<br /> <br /> It should only be moving to the right if you're taking damage of a higher severity that the resistant damage is currently linked to. So if you've taken 2 normal bashing, 1 resistant bashing, and 2 more normal bashing for:<br /> <br /> / / /R / /<br /> <br /> And then take two lethal, you get:<br /> <br /> X X / / /R / /<br /> <br /> If you have seven Health and you take four more Bashing in this situation, it starts to wrap around and would look like this:<br /> <br /> X X X X XR X /<br /> <br /> And then your friend uses magic to heal 4 lethal damage since you're in such bad shape. Healing starts on the right, but skips over the resistant damage, so you'd end up with:<br /> <br /> X XR /","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T04:07:04-08:00","id":1024211,"title":"","content":"Thanks that makes it alot clearer and if it was resistant bashing and the damage box is upgraded to lethat then it becomes resistant lethal correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T12:40:26-08:00","id":1024458,"title":"","content":"That's correct. If wrap can upgrade it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:20:05-07:00","id":1388132,"title":"","content":"What is a resistant bashing damage? What it implies? And how it can be healed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:59:05-07:00","id":1388148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023906-topic-for-discussion-damage-vs-resistant-damage?p=1388132#post1388132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is a resistant bashing damage? What it implies? And how it can be healed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Resistant damage is damage that cannot be healed by supernatural means, i.e. it can only be healed through the character's natural healing processes. It mostly shows up in Mage in the context of damage taken from containing a Paradox or scouring your Pattern for Mana.<br /> <br /> Why did you resurrect a four-year-old thread to ask a question you can find the answer to in the index of either edition's core rulebook?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T14:00:02-07:00","id":1388150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023906-topic-for-discussion-damage-vs-resistant-damage?p=1388132#post1388132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is a resistant bashing damage? What it implies? And how it can be healed?</div> </div> </div> </div>It can't be healed by magic. So it 'resists' magic healing. It happens when scouring your pattern (taking damage for Mana) or taking damage from Paradox. There's a sidebar about it in the upper right of page 223.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}